									<h2>The Value of a Wire Mesh Water Feature</h2><p>What’s great about using wire mesh in water features is the possibilities it creates for you. Maybe you want a mesh water wall in your courtyard to have a showpiece with calming ambiance. Perhaps you’re interested in the kind of mesh waterfall that can fit your modern landscape design. A mesh water feature offers a beautiful, functional solution with wire mesh that can be cut to size, welded, formed and framed to your needs. With that in mind, at Midwest Tropical, we get to know you and your space, so we can create the kind of water feature that works best to unify and add beauty to your location. Tell us what you are hoping to create and let our design team craft something perfect for you.</p>								</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-b99e980 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="b99e980" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<h2>Types of Custom Features Available With Wire Mesh</h2><p>Whether you’re designing an upscale hotel lobby, a business courtyard or landscaping at a commercial site, the right water feature can become a head turning centerpiece of style and value. That’s why we offer a wide range of mesh water features that can be catered to your specifications. Choose us to install:</p><ul><li>Mesh <a href="/interior-wall-waterfalls-for-the-interior-of-your-house/">waterfalls</a></li><li>Mesh <a href="/indoor-water-fountains/">fountains</a></li><li>Mesh <a href="/waterwalls/">water walls</a></li></ul><p>Each type of wire mesh water feature has distinct advantages that could make it ideal for you. To learn more about the added ambiance from our wire mesh water features, talk to our team. We’re here to customize water features to your needs.</p>								</div>
					</div>
		</div>
